{{also|bohemian}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|Bohemia|ian|lang=en}}

In sense of [[Romani]] and by association, marginalized artists, from {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|bohémien||person from [[Bohemia]], [[Romani]]|lang=fr}}, from {{term|Bohême||[[Bohemia]]|lang=fr}}. Regarding the sense evolution, compare {{term|gypsy|lang=en}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{context|countable|lang=en}} A native or resident of [[Bohemia]].
# {{context|uncountable|lang=en}} The [[dialect]] of the [[Czech]] [[language]] spoken in Bohemia.
# {{context|countable|archaic|lang=en}} A [[Gypsy]], a [[Romani]].
# {{context|countable|slang|lang=en}} A marginalized and impoverished young artist, or member of the urban [[literati]].

